The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
for (i = 1; i < fb->format->num_planes; i++) {
    plane_state->color_plane[i].offset = ~0xfff;
}
```
Reason:
The loop intended to set offsets for unused color planes was incorrectly limited by `fb->format->num_planes`, which did not account for the scenario where there could be more potential color planes (up to 4). As a result, the offsets for some unused planes were not set to `~0xfff`, leading to the use of stale offsets in subsequent calculations, particularly in `skl_check_main_surface()`.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
for (i = fb->format->num_planes; i < ARRAY_SIZE(plane_state->color_plane); i++) {
    plane_state->color_plane[i].offset = ~0xfff;
}
```
Reason:
This updated loop correctly sets the offsets for all unused color planes starting from `fb->format->num_planes` to the total size of `plane_state->color_plane`. By ensuring that all unused color planes are assigned the value `~0xfff`, it guarantees that the calculations in `skl_check_main_surface()` will use valid offsets, thus preventing potential inconsistencies and ensuring a non-negative `AUX_DIST`.

